From: Armada <noreply@armada.local>
Subject: [PATCH] pinctrl: qcom: sm8650-lpass-lpi: suspend across system sleep

The LPI pin controller holds the LPASS_HW_MACRO/LPASS_HW_DCODEC votes
while it is runtime active, and it is resumed whenever a pin state
changes. The SoundWire links and the LPASS macros select their sleep
pin states during system suspend, which resumes it after the PM core has
already blocked runtime suspend, so it stays active - and keeps both
votes - for the whole sleep. The ADSP then keeps its CX collapse vote.
On the Odin 3 (SM8750) the AOP reported the AUDIO DRV blocking CX
collapse through every s2idle even with 0630 in place: the macros
dropped their references, but this device kept the last one.

Force it into runtime suspend for system sleep. It supplies both
SoundWire links, so device links order it after them on suspend and
before them on resume.
---
--- a/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm8650-lpass-lpi.c
+++ b/drivers/pinctrl/qcom/pinctrl-sm8650-lpass-lpi.c
@@ -220,6 +220,7 @@ static const struct of_device_id lpi_pinctrl_of_match[] = {
 MODULE_DEVICE_TABLE(of, lpi_pinctrl_of_match);
 
 static const struct dev_pm_ops lpi_pinctrl_pm_ops = {
+	SYSTEM_SLEEP_PM_OPS(pm_runtime_force_suspend, pm_runtime_force_resume)
 	RUNTIME_PM_OPS(pm_clk_suspend, pm_clk_resume, NULL)
 };
 
